Description: Check audit_setloginuid's result
 Debian 13's libaudit declares it warn_unused_result, which fails the
 -Werror build. A failure is logged; the mapping still proceeds.
Author: NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-06
---
diff --git a/map_tacplus_user.c b/map_tacplus_user.c
index 7911f29..26392e2 100644
--- a/map_tacplus_user.c
+++ b/map_tacplus_user.c
@@ -599,7 +599,8 @@ recheck:
          * login, etc. because we need the info earlier than it is really
          * possible via the normal pam auth/session sequencing.
          */
-        audit_setloginuid(islocal?luid:tuid); /* set auid */
+        if (audit_setloginuid(islocal?luid:tuid) < 0) /* set auid */
+            syslog(LOG_WARNING, "audit_setloginuid failed: %m");
         /*
          * if USERHOMEDIR is set, we'll save that flag, and libnss-tacplus
          *  will return the login name in the pw_dir field replacing the
